  "plain": "Charles Hall, a man who says he spent years in contact with aliens while serving at a US air base and who wrote a book called The Valley of the Grays, talks about Roswell, the 1947 crash in New Mexico that many say involved an alien craft. Hall says there were two saucers there, and that what looked like melted rocks was really their fiber optics, cables that carry light, which had overheated and melted. If true, it would explain odd debris as the remains of advanced machines."
